SUMMARY:Tie One On Day
DESCRIPTION:Tie One On Day falls on the day before Thanksgiving\, which put
 s it on November 25 in 2026\, and despite the name it has nothing to do wi
 th drinking. The "one" is an apron. EllynAnne Geisel\, a Colorado writer a
 nd apron collector\, began the day after she wrapped a baked good in an ap
 ron\, tucked in a note\, and gave it to a neighbor who was having a hard t
 ime.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/tie-one-on-day/
URL;VALUE=URI:https://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/tie-one-on-day/
CATEGORIES:Celebration
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
